n years where  everything kicks off properly and but  unfortunately the last few weeks with  everything booked for this christmas  we've now been hit with these challenges  where we have to put several several  measures in place um  which is has never really been done  because um we haven't had the chance to  have the events in the last two years  you've been doing one or two fancy pants  parties in your time though aren't you  yeah the odd one yeah so here and there  um obviously we have a lot of clients  celebrities are not like the only  clients that we do and but yeah we've  done some some nice things for a few top  celebrities  um i think we've got a bit of a clue  about one of them let's have a quick  there you go um fantastic  you can't reveal too much more than that  i know but good for you hopefully things  will get back to normal before too long  thank you so much for joining us steve  thanks for having me  what about wedding plans what about  people who are getting married at this  time of year what are they allowed to do  and not do let's talk about that in more  detail and sarah hayward is with us um  hi sarah it must be so challenging for  people uk weddings task force and luxury  wedding planner as well of course um can  they just what roles do they have to  abide by  at the moment there are no restrictions  on weddings but  since we returned to work in july and  you'll probably recall weddings were  pretty much off the table for most of  the pandemic for a little while we were  able to do weddings of 15 people  and then 30 people but we really got  back to work mid july  we've been managing um the backlog  um so now as well as the weddings that  were planned we're obviously busy doing  the backlog of weddings uh over 18  months of cancellations and  postponements  so people are being careful um we're not  seeing um  postponements and cancellations at the  moment and of course anyone who's booked  a wedding for between now and christmas  it's all plan